{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789825913,"nonce":"bz0P8dEh3CGS4BF1DKyRxdDvXTU=","title":"Lua: runtime error messages lack the variable description","message":"Lua's luaG_typeerror appends varinfo to type errors: attempt to index a nil value (local 'x'), (global 'x'), (upvalue 'x'), (field 'x'), (constant 'x'), (method 'x'); arithmetic and concatenation pick the offending operand at runtime. The frontend knows the description at the site; the library raises the bare message.\n\nPlan: the check after a fallible call runs on the error path only, so it can annotate there: zb_hook_raise marks the pending message annotatable, the site's check appends its suffix (two suffixes for a binary operator, chosen by an operand index the library sets when it raises), and every check clears the mark so a deeper site's error is not annotated twice.\n\nAlso here: ipairs() with no argument says (value expected) since it takes any value; the checkers say (table expected, got nil). Absent and nil are the same box; got no value vs got nil is approximate.","files":null}]}